cards.front:
Refactor the following nested conditional using `elif` statements to achieve the same logic, assuming `score` is an integer.
```python
score = 75
if score >= 90:
    print("Grade A")
else:
    if score >= 80:
        print("Grade B")
    else:
        if score >= 70:
            print("Grade C")
        else:
            print("Grade F")
```

cards.back:
```python
score = 75
if score >= 90:
    print("Grade A")
elif score >= 80:
    print("Grade B")
elif score >= 70:
    print("Grade C")
else:
    print("Grade F")
```
This refactoring improves readability by flattening the conditional structure when evaluating mutually exclusive conditions.

